-- BizApps Common v5.51.x -- Metadata_Sync (one per release)
-- =============================================================================================
-- Generated by `mj sync push --dir metadata --exclude users --ci` (MJ CLI 6.1.5) against a
-- database built from migrations ONLY: MJ core 6.1.5, then this app's migrations at `next`.
-- Push result: 6 created, 63 updated, 247 unchanged, 0 errors. Checked column by column against a
-- copy of the database taken before the push; every change traces to metadata/, none reverts a
-- migration.
--
-- SHIPS:
--   * 59 EntityField updates -- the form layout (metadata/entity-fields/.form-layout.json):
--     Category, GeneratedFormSection, DisplayName and IncludeInGeneratedForm, with the matching
--     AutoUpdate* flags off so CodeGen keeps them.
--   * Entity Settings (metadata/entity-settings/.field-categories.json): FieldCategoryInfo created
--     on three entities; FieldCategoryInfo and FieldCategoryIcons values updated on Organizations.
--   * Generated Codes (metadata/generated-codes/.validators.json): ValidateEffectiveToAfterEffectiveFrom,
--     ValidateCapturedContentAndEncryptionKeyCoexistence, ValidateExternalIdAndSourceSystemCoexistence.
--   * Query `Common: Directory Dashboard Summary`: SQL and TechnicalDescription (business-day people
--     counts through fnBusinessDayOf).
--
-- HELD BACK, as in 5.48 -- field-level security for People (#186). The push turns on
-- Entity.EnableFieldLevelSecurity for People and, as MJ's reconcile, creates 105 Entity Field
-- Permission rows from this build database's own EntityPermission rows. Hosts upgrade by migration
-- only, so shipping those rows would apply this database's snapshot, not each host's; and with the
-- flag on, a field with no row is denied to every user. Both stay out until a host-side step applies
-- MJ's snapshot rule to each host's own permissions.
--
-- TRANSFORMS: `EXEC [${flyway:defaultSchema}]` -> `EXEC [${mjSchema}]` (every call is a core SP).
-- String values are untouched. Updates are by EntityField / EntitySetting / Query IDs pinned in
-- this app's migrations; Entity Setting creates are guarded on ID OR (EntityID, Name), Generated
-- Code creates on ID. Idempotent.
